A: Do you mean, in the same line you want to both count the elements that match the filter and output the filtered elements?
Just assign to a variable:
int count = 50 - arr.length - arr.filter(e -> e.indexOf("m") > -1).length;
System.out.println(count + " " + Arrays.toString(arr.filter(e -> e.indexOf("m") > -1)));
